{#
_modal.html.twig — the one dialog shell every modal in the app loads into.

One continuous surface. The header and footer used to be filled with bg-sunken,
which made every dialog read as a three-tone sandwich — the pattern the rest of
the app deliberately avoids: a pane is a single surface and uses hairline
border-line to divide, keeping bg-sunken for genuinely inset areas. The header
also rounded with rounded-t-2xl against a panel using rounded-pane, so the two
corners disagreed at every density setting.

Width is per-trigger. A label form wants to be narrow and a photo grid wants the
screen, so a trigger asks for a size and the controller applies it, rather than
every dialog inheriting whichever width suited the first one written.

The frame no longer scrolls: it is a flex column, so loaded content decides what
scrolls inside it. That is what lets the picker keep its own header and footer
still while only the results move.
#}

{# ── Backdrop + dialog wrapper ─────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
<div
    id="modal-backdrop"
    hidden
    data-ui--modal-dialog
    data-controller="ui--modal"
    data-action="click->ui--modal#backdropClick ui--modal:close->ui--modal#close"
    role="dialog"
    aria-modal="true"
    aria-labelledby="modal-title"
    class="
        fixed inset-0 z-50
        flex items-center justify-center
        bg-black/50 backdrop-blur-sm
        p-3 sm:p-6
    "
>
    {# ── Dialog panel ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# The size map lives here rather than in the controller so Tailwind sees
       these class names while scanning templates; a preset referenced only from
       JavaScript risks being purged out of the build. #}
    <div
        data-ui--modal-panel
        data-ui--modal-sizes='{"form":"max-w-lg","wide":"max-w-3xl","full":"max-w-6xl"}'
        class="
            relative w-full max-w-lg
            pane-flat
            shadow-float
            flex flex-col
            max-h-[92vh]
            overflow-hidden
        "
    >

        {# ── Header ──
           No fill and no rule: the title sits on the same surface as the body
           and the spacing does the separating. #}
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 px-6 pt-5 pb-4 shrink-0">
            <h2
                id="modal-title"
                data-ui--modal-title
                class="text-base font-semibold text-ink truncate"
            >
                {# Filled dynamically by the Stimulus controller or by the loaded frame #}
            </h2>

            <button
                type="button"
                data-action="click->ui--modal#close"
                aria-label="{{ 'modal.close'|trans }}"
                class="
                    ml-auto -mr-1 w-8 h-8 flex items-center justify-center rounded-lg
                    text-ink-faint
                    hover:text-ink
                    hover:bg-hover
                    transition-colors focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent
                "
            >
                <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark text-sm" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </button>
        </div>

        {# ── Turbo Frame — Turbo loads the form here ──────────────────────────── #}
        <turbo-frame
            id="modal"
            class="flex-1 min-h-0 flex flex-col"
            loading="lazy"
        >
            <div
                data-ui--modal-loading
                class="flex items-center justify-center h-32 text-ink-faint"
                aria-live="polite"
                aria-label="{{ 'modal.loading'|trans }}"
            >
                <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-notch fa-spin text-2xl" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            </div>
        </turbo-frame>

    </div>{# /panel #}
</div>{# /backdrop #}
